t of that item. Cross-item evidence... rule 6 says evidence must appear in source (of that item) or source_context. So evidence for Q004 must be \"Tales of the Spellblaze\". Hmm, that constrains. I'll use evidence \"Tales of the Spellblaze\" and mention in correction that source has no chapter count. The claim: adding \"七章\" unsupported by source. Verdict: since no evidence within the item supports \"seven\", it's an unsupported addition. Rule 3 protects only additions compatible with visible evidence and not judgeable wrong — Q005 makes it judgeable wrong. So FINDING, evidence \"Tales of the Spellblaze\" (source contains no number). I'll phrase correction: \"魔法大爆炸的故事（删除无据的'七章'）\".\n\nNow Q005 reconsider: \"Learned\" → \"阅读了\" — reading ≠ learning. This is a common localization choice. I'll report UNCERTAIN ACTION? Or leave empty. \"Learned the eight chapters\" — you learned the contents. \"阅读了...文献\" — read. The achievement is about learning. I'll include UNCERTAIN: claim ACTION, target_span \"阅读了\", correction \"习得了/学会了\", evidence \"Learned the eight chapters\". Hmm, is it substantive? Mildly. I'll include as UNCERTAIN.\n\nQ006: report UNCERTAIN SCOPE for \"主线\". Actually maybe FINDING? \"Quest\" generic → \"主线任务\" adds \"main\" which excludes side quests. For a generic message, this narrows. But maybe this string is only used for main quest in the game — can't know. UNCERTAIN SCOPE, target_span \"主线任务\", correction \"任务\".\n\nQ008: report the clipboard omission as FINDING? \"Click to copy to clipboard.\" → \"点击复制。\" The omission of \"剪贴板\" — target omits destination. Is it substantive? It's a small but objective omission. Rule 3 protects additions, not omissions. Omission of \"to clipboard\" — I'd report UNCERTAIN OMISSION. Also \"they\" → \"你们\": report? \"这样他们也可以用同一套技能游玩\" would be literal. \"你们\" changes subject. I'll report UNCERTAIN SUBJECT for \"这样你们可以用同一套技能组合进行游玩\"。Hmm, max 4 candidates; fine with 2.\n\nActually, let me reconsider whether to over-report. 